facts=[("Series","Tied 2-2, best of seven"),("Game 1, Oct 12","Guardians 7, Rays 3 (at Tampa Bay)"),("Game 2, Oct 13","Rays 3, Guardians 1 (at Tampa Bay)"),("Game 3, Oct 15","Guardians 3, Rays 2 (at Cleveland)"),("Game 4, Oct 17","Rays 7, Guardians 3 (at Cleveland, after a Friday rainout)"),("Game 5","Sun Oct 18, 5:08 p.m. ET, Cleveland. Parker Messick vs. Drew Rasmussen"),("Game 6","Mon Oct 19, 8 p.m. ET, Tropicana Field, St. Petersburg"),("Game 7 (if needed)","Tue Oct 20, 8 p.m. ET, Tropicana Field"),("TV","TBS, truTV, HBO Max; UniMas in Spanish"),("Winner plays","Milwaukee Brewers, World Series Game 1 on Fri Oct 23 on FOX")],
body=f'''<h2>How we got here</h2><p>Tampa Bay was the top team in the American League at 98-64, and Cleveland (85-77) came in as the underdog after a comeback against the White Sox in the Division Series. The Guardians stole Game 1 on the road, the Rays answered behind Freddy Peralta in Game 2, and rookie Petey Halpin's two-run homer won Game 3 for Cleveland. Then the rain came. Friday's Game 4 was postponed, and on Saturday the Rays turned two Cleveland errors into runs, with Jonathan Aranda's seventh-inning single and a Yandy D&iacute;az two-run homer in the ninth sealing it.</p>
<h2>Why Game 5 matters so much</h2><p>Per MLB.com research, when a best-of-seven series is tied 2-2, the Game 5 winner has gone on to win the series 46 of 69 times, about 67%. The twist: Tampa Bay hosts Games 6 and 7, so a Cleveland win today means the Guardians need just one more on the road, while a Rays win sends them home needing one of two.</p>
<h2>Our take</h2><p>This has been a pitching-and-defense series, with no team scoring more than seven runs and two of four games decided by a run or two. Whoever avoids the mistakes tonight probably wins. Either way, the Brewers get a well-rested look at the winner.</p>
<h2>Keep going</h2><ul><li><a href="../world-series-2026/">World Series 2026: dates, TV and the Brewers</a></li><li><a href="../mlb-nlcs-dodgers-brewers/">How the Brewers swept the Dodgers</a></li><li><a href="../mlb-postseason/">The full MLB postseason hub</a></li><li><a href="{R2}blog/brewers-world-series-2026-explained/">Why Milwaukee's run is a big deal</a></li><li><a href="../wnba-finals-2026/">Also tonight-ish: the WNBA Finals</a></li></ul>'''+follow("ALCS"),
