body=f'''<h2>What it's about (no spoilers)</h2><p>Jason drowns at camp, his body is never found, and nine months later Pam is still not okay. When body parts start turning up in the woods, the police chief's journalist sister starts pulling on a conspiracy thread, and Pam's own past turns out to be a lot darker than the town's lunch lady should have. Variety calls it more psychological thriller than straight slasher, with plenty of gore.</p>
<h2>The episode titles are a love letter</h2><p>Fans clocked this fast: episodes include <b>"A New Beginning," "The New Blood," "Friday..."</b> and <b>"The Final Chapter,"</b> which echo the titles of Friday the 13th sequels. Variety singles out Episode 7, "Friday...," a 1959-set flashback, as the best of the bunch.</p>
<table><tr><th>Ep</th><th>Title</th></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>A New Beginning</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>The New Blood</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Kill Them, Mommy</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Friday...</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>The Final Chapter</td></tr></table><p class="src">Episode titles per Rotten Tomatoes' season listing.</p>
<h2>What critics and fans say</h2><p>The split is pretty clean. Critics love Cardellini and the craft, and some find the middle episodes slow and the conspiracy overstuffed. The Guardian gave it 2 out of 5; Peter Travers gave it 3 out of 4. Audience scores are running higher than critics.</p>
<h2>More spooky-season picks</h2><ul><li><a href="{R2}blog/crystal-lake-peacock-explained/">Our Crystal Lake explainer: why everyone's binging it</a></li><li><a href="{R2}pop-culture/halloween-costumes-2026/">Halloween costumes 2026: what people are wearing</a></li><li><a href="../marvel/">VisionQuest and the rest of Marvel on TV</a></li><li><a href="{R2}movies/sunrise-on-the-reaping-guide/">Sunrise on the Reaping: tickets and watch order</a></li><li><a href="../">Everything trending in TV and streaming</a></li></ul>'''+follow("CrystalLake"),
